pe": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "isolation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the state of being or feeling alone, isolated", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I don't work well in isolation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about work responsibilities.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to reckon", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bthink or \u200bbelieve", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I reckon I've been most productive in quiet places.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to come along", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to progress", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How are things coming along?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "significant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "important", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Nothing really significant yet. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to hold up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to delay", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you are late, it holds up the whole production schedule.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to forge ahead ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bsuddenly make a lot of \u200bprogress with something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: As soon as I finish this chapter, I'll forge ahead with the the next one.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "shortly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "soon", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I'll finish up the editing shortly, and then I can begin the layout whenever you want.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "  Adverbial Clauses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " An adverbial clause is two or more words that serve the function of an adverb. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbs of Place</span><br/> An adverb of place identifies where something happens. It usually begins with a preposition (e.g., <span class=\"italic\">in</span>, <span class=\"italic\">on</span>, <span class=\"italic\">near</span>) or one of the following subordinating conjunctions: <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">anywhere</span>, <span class=\"strong\"><span class=\"italic\">everywhere</span>, <span class=\"italic\">where</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">wherever</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">In a house <span class=\"strong\">where</span> everything is in order, nobody loses anything.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbs of Manner</span><br/> An adverb of manner explains the way something is done. It usually starts with one of the following subordinating conjunctions:<span class=\"strong\"> <span class=\"italic\">as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">like</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">the way</span>. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li><span class=\"italic\">He laughs<span class=\"strong\"> like</span> a hyena. <li><span class=\"italic\">You are looking at me<span class=\"strong\"> the way </span>a child looks at a ghost. </li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">As soon as</span> I complete the report, I'll answer your question.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I'll continue working on this novel <span class=\"strong\">until</span> it wins the Nobel prize.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We can start the meeting <span class=\"strong\">whenever</span> it is most convenient for you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbs of Time</span><br/> An adverb of manner explains when something happens. It usually starts with one of the following subordinating conjunctions:<span class=\"strong\"> <span class=\"italic\">as soon as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">when</span>, <span class=\"italic\">until</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">whenever</span>.</span>    <ul><li><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Whenever </span></span>I call, he's busy. <li><span class=\"italic\">I will send the document<span class=\"strong\"> as soon as</span> I get to the office. </span> </li></ul> <br><span class=\"strong\"> Until </span>means \u2013 up to that time,  so, until 4 p.m. means up to 4p.m. but not after.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Present Perfect with Report or Comment Phrases", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about past events that have a connection to the future. <br/> You can use the Present Perfect tense with other verbs to report or comment on events.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use verbs such as <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">reckon, understand, suppose, guess</span></span>  and <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">imagine</span></span>  to communicate your thoughts and to report about something that happened in the past and has a connection to the present. <br/><br/> The structure is:<br/><br/> subject + report/comment verb+ (that) + Present Perfect<br/><br/> For example:<br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">understand</span> (that) you have done</span> a lot of editing in previous jobs.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">suppose</span>   that I have worked on several different documents in the past.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">reckon</span>   I've been most productive in quiet places, but I do like to have people around.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">guess</span>   I've always worked best with the energy of being around people. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">imagine </span>  that you have chased lots of copy editors for their work.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "With a partner, brainstorm adjectives to describe good and bad qualities in a manager.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Make a list of things that a good manager should and shouldn't do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a paragraph describing the personality and behavior of a good manager.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Exchange paragraphs with another group and see if you had any of the same ideas.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I brainstorm qualities of a good manager.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I list things a manager should and shouldn't do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a paragraph describing a good manager.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I compare my paragraph with another group.", "type": "text"}]}]}